{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates Java code to GNU C++11 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following Java 8 code to GNU C++11 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original Java 8 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\nimport java.util.stream.*;\n\npublic class lets_do {\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        String all = br.lines().collect(Collectors.joining(\" \"));\n        int[] nums = Arrays.stream(all.trim().split(\"\\\\s+\")).mapToInt(Integer::parseInt).toArray();\n        int n = nums[0];\n        int b = nums[1];\n        int[] a = Arrays.copyOfRange(nums, 2, 2 + n);\n        int[] pe = new int[n];\n        int[] po = new int[n];\n        int even = 0, odd = 0;\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {\n            if ((a[i] & 1) == 0) even++;\n            else odd++;\n            pe[i] = even;\n            po[i] = odd;\n        }\n        int[] w = IntStream.range(1, n - 2)\n                .filter(i -> (i & 1) == 1 && pe[i] == po[i])\n                .map(i -> Math.abs(a[i + 1] - a[i]))\n                .toArray();\n        int[] dp = new int[b + 1];\n        for (int weight : w) {\n            for (int cap = b; cap >= weight; cap--) {\n                dp[cap] = Math.max(dp[cap], dp[cap - weight] + 1);\n            }\n        }\n        System.out.println(dp[b]);\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <sstream>\n#include <string>\n#include <vector>\n#include <algorithm>\n#include <cmath>\n\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    // Read all input lines and join with spaces\n    string all;\n    string line;\n    while (getline(cin, line)) {\n        all += line + \" \";\n    }\n    \n    // Parse integers from the joined string\n    stringstream ss(all);\n    vector<int> nums;\n    int num;\n    while (ss >> num) {\n        nums.push_back(num);\n    }\n    \n    // First two numbers: n and b\n    int n = nums[0];\n    int b = nums[1];\n    \n    // Next n numbers: array a\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        a[i] = nums[2 + i];\n    }\n    \n    // Prefix counts of even and odd numbers\n    vector<int> pe(n), po(n);\n    int even = 0, odd = 0;\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        if ((a[i] & 1) == 0) even++;\n        else odd++;\n        pe[i] = even;\n        po[i] = odd;\n    }\n    \n    // Compute weights: indices i from 1 to n-3 inclusive where i is odd and pe[i]==po[i]\n    vector<int> w;\n    for (int i = 1; i < n - 2; ++i) {\n        if ((i & 1) == 1 && pe[i] == po[i]) {\n            w.push_back(abs(a[i + 1] - a[i]));\n        }\n    }\n    \n    // 0/1 knapsack: maximize number of cuts with total cost <= b\n    vector<int> dp(b + 1, 0);\n    for (int weight : w) {\n        for (int cap = b; cap >= weight; --cap) {\n            dp[cap] = max(dp[cap], dp[cap - weight] + 1);\n        }\n    }\n    \n    cout << dp[b] << endl;\n    \n    return 0;\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.06309696286916733, -3.2186455882765586e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00024625606